NFS(Network File System.)
Linux machines sharing folders. Linux/Unix file-sharing protocol. Client mounts remote directory.

Without NFS->
Machine A: /data/reports
Machine B cannot access.

With NFS->
Machine A shares folder.
Machine B mounts it:

Shell:
mount -t nfs server:/data /mnt/data
mount server:/reports /mnt/reports

Now it feels local.

Example:
100 application servers.
Need same configuration files.
Instead of copying to every server: NFS Share
All servers read from one place.

Why Companies Love NFS?
Easy.Centralized.No duplicate files.

